## Additional instructions:
    - PROCEED LIKE A SENIOR DEVELOPER. I mean proceed like a 10x engineer!
    - DO NOT STOP UNTIL COMPLETE UNDER ANY CIRCUMSTANCES!
Do not stop working on current task until you've implemented this feature fully and completely!!
    - THREE REASONING PARAGRAPHS:
Start by writing three reasoning paragraphs analyzing what the error might be. **Do not jump to conclusions.**
    - DO NOT DELETE COMMENTS  
Do not delete comments. **Always comment the code you are writing. Also, always set up a proper documentation.**
    - START WITH UNCERTAINTY  
You should start 3 reasoning paragraphs with lots of uncertainty and slowly gain confidence as you think about the item more.
    - ONLY INCLUDE TRULY NECESSARY STEPS  
Break large change into the required steps. Only include the truly necessary steps.
    - ALWAYS WRITE COMMENTS FOR YOUR CODE!
    - Always use logging in order to be able to debug the code in the future.
